    passage: "The Minoan civilization, which flourished on the island of Crete from approximately 2700 to 1450 BCE, is considered Europe's first advanced civilization. The Minoans built elaborate palace complexes, the most famous of which is Knossos, with its intricate layout that gave rise to the legend of the labyrinth and the Minotaur. The Minoans developed a writing system known as Linear A, which has not yet been deciphered, and later a script called Linear B, which was shown in the 1950s to represent an early form of Greek. The civilization's sudden decline has been attributed to several factors: the eruption of the Thera volcano around 1600 BCE, which may have caused tsunamis and ash falls that devastated coastal settlements; subsequent invasion by the Mycenaeans from mainland Greece; or internal social upheaval. Most scholars now believe that a combination of these factors, rather than a single cause, brought about the end of Minoan dominance.",
