    passage: "The cyanobacterium Prochlorococcus is the most abundant photosynthetic organism on Earth, with an estimated three octillion individuals—roughly equivalent to the number of stars in the visible universe. Discovered only in 1986, this microscopic organism is found throughout the world's oceans, from the surface down to depths of about 200 meters. Prochlorococcus accounts for an estimated 20 percent of the oxygen produced on Earth each year, making it a critical contributor to the planet's atmosphere. Despite its immense ecological importance, Prochlorococcus was not discovered earlier because it is extremely small—about one-fiftieth the size of a typical bacterium—and because its unique pigment composition made it invisible to the fluorescent detection methods that scientists were using at the time.",
